TITLE='Authentic title "WTF Just Happened To The Housing Market?!" is a shock-question frame. The script answers it with a causal sequence (zero rates and QE, pandemic migration, the 2022-23 hiking cycle, rate lock-in, underbuilding, tariffs), so the promise is delivered. The title implies a sudden event; the script describes a multi-year freeze.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background: the recurring cartoon man, mouth open; "IT\'S OVER..." in heavy black capitals; a red zig-zag line falling across a grid onto a cracked house with a red down arrow and rubble. At 320x180 the words, the chart and the house read clearly. The image signals a price crash, but the script says prices are near all-time highs and explicitly rejects a 2008-style crash ("Is this 2008? No."). Packaging contradicts the thesis.'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator housing explainer: paradox hook (lowest sales since 1995 at near-record prices), payment arithmetic, the 2020-21 cheap-money and migration surge, the 2022-23 hiking cycle, affordability gap, rate lock-in, a composite buyer (Maya), the emotional experience and first-time buyer statistics, underbuilding and tariffs, why it is not 2008, rate outlook and lock-in fade, the risk that fast rate cuts raise prices, and decision rules (28-30% of gross, 7-year horizon, rent-and-invest, builder buy-downs). Most payment arithmetic reproduces; the current median price is about $20,000 high, the 46% rise is miscalculated, and several research figures differ from their published sources.'
BEATS=['Hook: fewer sales, higher prices.','Payment gap at 2.65% vs 6.5%.','2020: zero rates and QE.','Pandemic migration and price surge.','2022-23 hikes and rate path.','Affordability gap and sales collapse.','Rate lock-in.','Maya composite budget.','Emotional experience; first-time buyers at 40.','Underbuilding, starter homes, tariffs.','Why it is not 2008.','Rate outlook and lock-in fade.','Decision rules and close.']
